<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Limits of Polynomials — combining limits with the sum and constant-multiple laws</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Given that \( \displaystyle\lim_{x\to {@aa@}} f(x) = {@Lf@} \) and \( \displaystyle\lim_{x\to {@aa@}} g(x) = {@Lg@} \), evaluate</p>
<p>\[ \lim_{x\to {@aa@}} \big( {@ca@}f(x) + {@cb@}g(x) \big). \]</p>
<div>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Two limit laws do the work here. The <strong>sum rule</strong> says the limit of a sum is the sum of the limits, and the <strong>constant multiple rule</strong> says a constant factor can be taken outside the limit:</p>
\[ \lim_{x\to {@aa@}}\big({@ca@}f(x)+{@cb@}g(x)\big) = {@ca@}\lim_{x\to {@aa@}}f(x) + {@cb@}\lim_{x\to {@aa@}}g(x) = {@ca@}\times({@Lf@})+{@cb@}\times({@Lg@}) = {@ta@}. \]
<p>Keep the constant multipliers \({@ca@}\) and \({@cb@}\), and add the two scaled limits rather than multiplying them.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber/>
    <stackversion>
      <text>2026063000</text>
    </stackversion>
    <questionvariables>
      <text>aa: rand_with_prohib(1,5,[]);
Lf: rand_with_prohib(-9,9,[0]);
ca: rand_with_prohib(2,5,[]);
cb: rand_with_prohib(2,5,[]);
/* Lg is chosen so that the answer, both diagnostic values and the generic
   wrong test value ta+1 are pairwise distinct, and the answer is not 0 or 1 or -1.
   Each prohibited value solves one coincidence equation for Lg (non-integers never match).
   Brute-force checked over the whole domain: no collisions, never an empty choice. */
Lg: rand_with_prohib(-9,9,[0, -(ca-1)*Lf/(cb-1), ca*Lf/(ca*cb*Lf-cb), Lf/(ca*cb*Lf-1), -ca*Lf/cb, (1-ca*Lf)/cb, (-1-ca*Lf)/cb, (-1-(ca-1)*Lf)/(cb-1), (ca*Lf+1)/(ca*cb*Lf-cb)]);
ta: ca*Lf + cb*Lg;
wrong_ignorecoef: Lf + Lg;
wrong_multiplyall: ca*Lf*cb*Lg;</text>
    </questionvariables>
    <specificfeedback format="html">
      <text>[[feedback:prt1]]</text>
